Subject: [PATCH] nbd-proxy: recover orphan gadget before connecting a new NBD

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [CEB-GNRD virtual media recovery]

The hook must inspect old kernel/client state before the new client starts.
If the existing gadget cannot safely be reclaimed, reject the new session
without changing the old NBD connection or USB binding.

--- a/nbd-proxy.c
+++ b/nbd-proxy.c
@@ -928,4 +928,8 @@
     fprintf(stderr, "virtual-media[%s,pid=%ld]: session start device=%s timeout=%d\n", ctx->config->name, (long)getpid(), ctx->config->nbd_device, ctx->nbd_timeout);
+    rc = run_state_hook(ctx, "recover", true);
+    if (rc)
+        goto out_free;
+
     rc = open_nbd_socket(ctx);
     if (rc)
         goto out_free;
